## Context
Rule `rules/coding-python.md` (Environment principles and rules, added by PR 1634, which merges before this tracker) states one uv-based environment practice: dependencies in pyproject.toml with a committed uv.lock, no pip, one `RUN` prefix in the Makefile and no PYTHON variable. On 2026-10-23 the alignment check below ran on ten Python repos (in ~/CNRS/code: askMinh, carto chercheurs département SSM IP, DOIfetch, fs-housekeeper, llm_benchmarks, maiba, Music Library Clinic, ThinkTanksSurveyor, VN-Power-Scenario; plus sen-causal-reading; selected as the directories with a top-level pyproject.toml or requirements.txt; not counted: natu, a 2020 setup.py library, and directories with Python but neither file, such as search-works-for-zotero, Costs-and-Benefits-Cofiring-VN and Household electricity, which a later sweep may add): five print ok, five do not: sen-causal-reading (its own ticket 0083 and PR, on its branch t0083-uv-env in ~/CNRS/papiers/actif/sen-causal-reading) and the four children below. Impact is real only for sen-causal-reading, where `project-state.py --tests` reported a false failure (author's observation, 2026-10-23; not reproduced in review); the four children are deviations, not breakages, ticketed at the author's request (2026-10-23) although they sit under the severity floor.

## Children
- 1207 askMinh (moved: askMinh tickets/0001, open there; branch t0001-uv-env ready for the author's merge, 2026-10-27)
- 1208 VN-Power-Scenario (closed, dropped by the author 2026-10-23: left alone; draft PR 27 on its origin stays open, the check prints NOT ok on master and the 11 regression tests await the author's decision; nothing was pushed to the collaborator's fork)
- 1209 ThinkTanksSurveyor (closed, done 2026-10-23: now a git repository with no remote, uv-aligned and merged locally on main; the check prints `ok`)
- 1210 fs-housekeeper (moved: fs-housekeeper tickets/0001, closed there 2026-10-27, merged 0f7f11c, check ok)
- sen-causal-reading: ticket 0083 in that repo, closed there; PR 87 merged 2026-10-23 (requirements.txt removed, ruff kept at 0.15 by the author); the alignment check prints `ok` there

## Alignment check
One line per repo, run from the repo root; prints `ok` when aligned. It took 0.2 s over all ten repos on 2026-10-23. The check is necessary, not sufficient: it does not see a Makefile that runs Python tools without the `RUN` prefix, so each child's exit criteria still rule.
```
[ -f pyproject.toml ] && [ -f uv.lock ] && ! grep -qE "^[[:space:]]*(export[[:space:]]+)?PYTHON[[:space:]]*[?:]?=" Makefile 2>/dev/null && ! grep -rqs "pip install" Makefile README.md docs && { [ ! -f requirements.txt ] || head -1 requirements.txt | grep -q autogenerated; } && echo ok
```
A requirements.txt is accepted only when its first line says it is autogenerated by uv; sen-causal-reading chose to drop the file (author, 2026-10-23), so none of the ten repos relies on this exception today.

## Verification cadence
No new probe in project-state.py (author, 2026-10-23). Because the check is that fast, it belongs to /lair if it is run periodically; whether /lair gains a step for it is open. Until then this tracker, open while any child is open, is the reminder.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Children closed, each with the check printing `ok` or a stated reason it does not apply: 1208 (dropped) and 1209 (done) are closed; 1207 and 1210 are still open in their own repos (askMinh and fs-housekeeper tickets/0001)
- [x] sen-causal-reading ticket 0083 merged or dropped by its author (merged, PR 87, 2026-10-23)
- [ ] Integration: the check prints `ok`, and the child's exit criteria hold, in every repo not dropped
